1
00:00:00,760 --> 00:00:03,239
[♪♪♪]

2
00:00:03,239 --> 00:00:04,600
I'm Peppa Pig.

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:05,680
[SNORTS]

4
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:07,319
This is my little brother
George.

5
00:00:07,319 --> 00:00:08,280
[SNORTS]

6
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:09,680
This is Mummy Pig.

7
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:10,639
[SNORTS]

8
00:00:10,639 --> 00:00:11,959
And this is Daddy Pig.

9
00:00:11,959 --> 00:00:13,280
[SNORTS]

10
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:14,920
Peppa Pig.

11
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:15,760
[SNORTS]

12
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:20,119
[♪♪♪]

13
00:00:20,119 --> 00:00:22,720
PEPPA: Stars.

14
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:25,000
NARRATOR:
It is almost time for bed.

15
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,119
Mummy Pig, Daddy Pig and Peppa
are having mugs of hot milk.

16
00:00:29,119 --> 00:00:31,639
[SNORTS THEN GIGGLES]

17
00:00:31,639 --> 00:00:35,360
George, why are you dressed up
in that spacesuit?

18
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:37,360
You should be
in your pajamas.

19
00:00:37,360 --> 00:00:38,320
[GIGGLING]

20
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:39,559
NARRATOR:
George loves

21
00:00:39,559 --> 00:00:42,040
everything to do
with space.

22
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:43,600
Oh.
[GIGGLES]

23
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:46,360
George,
take your space helmet off

24
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:49,040
to drink your milk.

25
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:51,239
[SLURPS THEN BURPS]

26
00:00:51,239 --> 00:00:52,800
[ALL LAUGH]

27
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:55,080
Bedtime, little ones.

28
00:00:55,080 --> 00:00:57,559
[GEORGE &amp; PEPPA LAUGHING]

29
00:00:57,559 --> 00:01:00,640
NARRATOR:
At night, George likes
to listen to his space mobile.

30
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:02,599
[LULLABY MUSIC PLAYING
OVER MOBILE CHIMES)

31
00:01:02,599 --> 00:01:04,720
Not space again.

32
00:01:04,720 --> 00:01:05,720
[SIGHS]

33
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:07,200
It's boring.

34
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:09,440
Space isn't boring.

35
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:11,000
It's full of stars.

36
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,920
[SNORTS]
I can't see anything.

37
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:15,840
It's too dark.

38
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:19,000
It's easier to see the stars
from outside.

39
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Can we go outside now?

40
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:23,440
Peppa,
you're in your pajamas.

41
00:01:23,440 --> 00:01:27,119
Maybe if you put your coats on
over your pajamas,

42
00:01:27,119 --> 00:01:29,479
we could go outside
just this once.

43
00:01:29,479 --> 00:01:30,800
Hooray!
[SNORTS]

44
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:33,839
[♪♪♪]

45
00:01:33,839 --> 00:01:35,039
[GIGGLES]

46
00:01:35,039 --> 00:01:38,399
Daddy, why are you lying
on the ground?

47
00:01:38,399 --> 00:01:41,080
This is the best way
to see the stars.

48
00:01:41,080 --> 00:01:43,080
[PEPPA &amp; GEORGE LAUGHING]

49
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:44,720
DADDY PIG:
Look at these little stars.

50
00:01:44,720 --> 00:01:46,880
Imagine
you are joining the dots.

51
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:48,839
MUMMY PIG:
That's called the Big Dipper.

52
00:01:48,839 --> 00:01:50,399
PEPPA &amp; GEORGE:
Ooh.

53
00:01:50,399 --> 00:01:53,399
DADDY PIG: Yes.
And the two stars at the end

54
00:01:53,399 --> 00:01:55,320
point to the North Star.

55
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:57,000
PEPPA &amp; GEORGE:
Wow.

56
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,800
♪ North Star, North Star ♪

57
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:02,679
♪ Are you near
Or are you far? ♪

58
00:02:02,679 --> 00:02:05,759
♪ Can we get there
In the car? ♪

59
00:02:05,759 --> 00:02:07,880
Ho-ho-ho. No, Peppa.

60
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:10,359
The stars
are much too far away.

61
00:02:10,359 --> 00:02:13,120
Are they even further
than the seaside?

62
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:14,519
Oh, yes.

63
00:02:14,519 --> 00:02:17,920
But they look a lot closer
through a telescope.

64
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:20,280
Have we got a telly-scope?

65
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:21,640
[SNORTS]
No,

66
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:24,000
but Grandpa Pig
has a very good telescope.

67
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Can we go
to Grandpa Pig's house now?

68
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:29,840
Ho-ho-ho.
It's much too late.

69
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:31,959
[SNORTS]
Maybe we can go

70
00:02:31,959 --> 00:02:33,680
just this once, Daddy Pig.

71
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:34,760
Hooray.

72
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:36,359
NARRATOR:
It is the first time

73
00:02:36,359 --> 00:02:38,560
Peppa and George have been
in the car at night.

74
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:40,320
[♪♪♪]

75
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:43,959
[SNORTS]
Look, we're following
the North Star.

76
00:02:43,959 --> 00:02:45,239
[PEPPA CHUCKLES]

77
00:02:45,239 --> 00:02:48,079
♪ North Star, North Star ♪

78
00:02:48,079 --> 00:02:51,160
♪ Shining
With a twinkly glow ♪

79
00:02:51,160 --> 00:02:53,799
♪ Please show us
The way to go ♪

80
00:02:53,799 --> 00:02:55,120
[ALL LAUGH]

81
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:56,799
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George have arrived

82
00:02:56,799 --> 00:02:58,679
at Granny
and Grandpa Pig's house.

83
00:02:58,679 --> 00:02:59,760
Oh, dear.

84
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:01,799
I do hope
Grandpa and Granny Pig

85
00:03:01,799 --> 00:03:02,920
haven't gone to bed.

86
00:03:02,920 --> 00:03:04,959
[DOORBELL DINGS]

87
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:10,880
What are you doing here
at this hour?

88
00:03:10,880 --> 00:03:13,200
We want to see the stars.

89
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:14,799
Peppa and George were hoping

90
00:03:14,799 --> 00:03:16,760
they could look
through your telescope.

91
00:03:16,760 --> 00:03:19,679
I see. Very well.

92
00:03:19,679 --> 00:03:22,480
To the top of the house,
everyone.

93
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:24,799
[PEPPA &amp; GEORGE LAUGHING]

94
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:28,799
[SNORTS]
Here she is.

95
00:03:28,799 --> 00:03:30,359
Old Bess.

96
00:03:30,359 --> 00:03:31,679
BOTH:
Wow.

97
00:03:31,679 --> 00:03:33,359
NARRATOR:
Grandpa Pig's hobby

98
00:03:33,359 --> 00:03:35,119
is looking at the stars.

99
00:03:35,119 --> 00:03:39,200
Now,
who's for the first look?

100
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:40,760
Me, me, me!

101
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:44,200
Ooh. The North Star.

102
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:47,880
We sailors use it
to find our way home.

103
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:50,840
Daddy used it
to find his way here.

104
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:52,640
[ALL LAUGHING]

105
00:03:52,640 --> 00:03:54,640
[SNORTS]
Are there other things

106
00:03:54,640 --> 00:03:55,799
in the sky?

107
00:03:55,799 --> 00:04:00,119
Yes.
This is a planet called Saturn.

108
00:04:00,119 --> 00:04:03,679
PEPPA: Wow.
What are those pretty rings?

109
00:04:03,679 --> 00:04:06,959
GRANDPA PIG:
They are made of rock and ice.

110
00:04:06,959 --> 00:04:10,560
Saturn is very, very cold.

111
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:13,640
PEPPA: We could build
a snowman, George.

112
00:04:13,640 --> 00:04:15,679
[BOTH LAUGHING]

113
00:04:17,440 --> 00:04:19,519
[ALL LAUGHING]

114
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:22,840
Quick. Look.

115
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:24,400
Oh.

116
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:27,039
GRANDPA PIG:
It's a shooting star.

117
00:04:27,039 --> 00:04:28,719
You must make a wish.

118
00:04:28,719 --> 00:04:34,000
I wish that when George is old
enough to have his own rocket,

119
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,360
he will take me into space.
[SNORTS]

120
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:39,400
[BOTH LAUGHING]

121
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:48,520
[♪♪♪]

122
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:51,400
PEPPA:
Daddy Pig's Birthday.

123
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:53,840
NARRATOR:
Today is Daddy Pig's birthday.

124
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:55,080
[SNORTS]

125
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:56,840
NARRATOR:
Daddy Pig has to go to work.

126
00:04:56,840 --> 00:05:00,240
Daddy, I wish you didn't have
to work on your birthday.

127
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:02,039
Ha, ha. So do I.

128
00:05:02,039 --> 00:05:04,039
But I'll be home
as soon as I can.

129
00:05:04,039 --> 00:05:06,599
See you later.
ALL: See you later.

130
00:05:06,599 --> 00:05:08,599
[HORN HONKS]

131
00:05:08,599 --> 00:05:11,000
[SNORTS]
While Daddy Pig is at work,

132
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,960
we can get all
his birthday surprises ready.

133
00:05:13,960 --> 00:05:15,440
[BOTH LAUGH]

134
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:18,400
First, we'll make
Daddy's birthday cake.

135
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:22,400
We start with butter,
and sugar and flour.

136
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:24,919
Then we add an egg.

137
00:05:24,919 --> 00:05:27,000
And most important of all,

138
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,039
the chocolate bits.
BOTH: Ooh.

139
00:05:29,039 --> 00:05:31,440
NARRATOR:
Mummy Pig is making
a chocolate cake.

140
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:33,560
Daddy Pig loves
chocolate cake.

141
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:34,880
I give it a stir.

142
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:36,640
Mummy, can I stir?

143
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:37,880
Yes, Peppa.

144
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,800
NARRATOR:
Peppa loves stirring.

145
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:41,840
[SNORTS]

146
00:05:41,840 --> 00:05:43,200
NARRATOR:
George wants a go.

147
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:45,240
[BOTH LAUGHING]

148
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:46,599
[LAUGHS AND SNORTS]

149
00:05:46,599 --> 00:05:49,479
Okay, George,
that's enough stirring.

150
00:05:49,479 --> 00:05:52,159
There.
Daddy Pig's chocolate cake.

151
00:05:52,159 --> 00:05:54,120
PEPPA:
Hooray!

152
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:57,440
Now, we just have to bake it
in the oven.

153
00:05:57,440 --> 00:06:00,039
[SNORTS]
Mummy, can I lick the spoon?

154
00:06:00,039 --> 00:06:03,880
Yes. You can lick the spoon,
and George can lick the bowl.

155
00:06:03,880 --> 00:06:05,120
Yippee.
[GIGGLES]

156
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:07,479
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George love

157
00:06:07,479 --> 00:06:08,560
chocolate cake mixture.

158
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:10,240
[ALL LAUGHING]

159
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:12,760
Poor Daddy Pig,
he's missing all the fun.

160
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:16,599
Mummy, can I ring Daddy at work
and say, "Happy birthday"?

161
00:06:16,599 --> 00:06:18,560
That's a nice idea.

162
00:06:18,560 --> 00:06:20,799
[KEYPAD BEEPING]

163
00:06:20,799 --> 00:06:23,000
[LINE RINGS]

164
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,400
NARRATOR:
This is the office,
where Daddy Pig works.

165
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:28,680
Hello, Mr. Rabbit speaking.

166
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:32,479
May I speak to Daddy Pig,
please?

167
00:06:32,479 --> 00:06:36,000
Someone for you, Daddy Pig.
It sounds important.

168
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:38,799
[SNORTS]
Hello, Daddy Pig speaking.

169
00:06:38,799 --> 00:06:41,080
Happy birthday, Daddy!

170
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:43,760
[SNORTS]
Happy birthday!

171
00:06:43,760 --> 00:06:46,200
Ho, ho. Thank you, Peppa.

172
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:48,080
Don't be late home, Daddy.

173
00:06:48,080 --> 00:06:49,440
[SNORTS]
Bye-bye.

174
00:06:49,440 --> 00:06:50,680
Bye-Bye.

175
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:51,760
[BOTH BLOWING PARTY HORNS]

176
00:06:51,760 --> 00:06:54,159
BOTH:
Happy birthday, Daddy Pig.

177
00:06:54,159 --> 00:06:55,240
[CHUCKLES]

178
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:56,320
Thank you.

179
00:06:56,320 --> 00:06:58,080
[♪♪♪]

180
00:06:58,080 --> 00:07:00,039
[SNORTS]
There's just
one more thing

181
00:07:00,039 --> 00:07:01,560
to do
before Daddy gets home.

182
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:04,479
Yes.
Daddy's birthday surprise.

183
00:07:04,479 --> 00:07:05,719
[GIGGLES]

184
00:07:05,719 --> 00:07:09,840
Shh. George, remember,
it's a secret.

185
00:07:09,840 --> 00:07:10,840
Shh.

186
00:07:10,840 --> 00:07:12,680
[BOTH GIGGLE]

187
00:07:14,239 --> 00:07:16,880
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George have
buckets of water.

188
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:18,599
Mummy Pig has balloons.

189
00:07:18,599 --> 00:07:19,960
[PEPPA &amp; GEORGE LAUGHING]

190
00:07:19,960 --> 00:07:21,440
NARRATOR:
I wonder what Daddy Pig's

191
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:23,039
birthday surprise can be.

192
00:07:23,039 --> 00:07:24,960
[BOTH LAUGHING]

193
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:26,080
[CAR HORN HONKS]

194
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:27,239
Daddy's home.

195
00:07:27,239 --> 00:07:29,120
Quick. Back to the house.

196
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:32,760
NARRATOR:
Daddy Pig is home from work.

197
00:07:33,799 --> 00:07:36,239
ALL:
Happy birthday, Daddy Pig.

198
00:07:36,239 --> 00:07:37,239
[BLOWS PARTY HORN]

199
00:07:37,239 --> 00:07:38,239
[LAUGHS]

200
00:07:38,239 --> 00:07:39,960
Thank you, everyone.

201
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:42,799
[SNORTS]
Wow. What a lot of candles.

202
00:07:42,799 --> 00:07:46,680
That's because
you're very, very old, Daddy.

203
00:07:46,680 --> 00:07:47,799
[LAUGHS]

204
00:07:47,799 --> 00:07:49,440
[SNORTS]
You must blow out

205
00:07:49,440 --> 00:07:51,479
all your candles in one go.

206
00:07:51,479 --> 00:07:54,200
Ho, ho. I'll do my best.

207
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:56,359
[INHALES DEEPLY
THEN EXHALES AUDIBLY]

208
00:07:59,719 --> 00:08:00,960
ALL:
Hooray!

209
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:03,120
[SIGHS]
[ALL LAUGHING]

210
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:06,000
[SNORTS] And here's
your birthday present.

211
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,359
Thank you.

212
00:08:07,359 --> 00:08:09,400
[THUDDING]

213
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:12,159
New boots. Fantastic.

214
00:08:12,159 --> 00:08:13,479
Let's try them out.

215
00:08:13,479 --> 00:08:15,479
[♪♪♪]

216
00:08:15,479 --> 00:08:18,400
NARRATOR:
Peppa, George and Mummy Pig
are wearing their boots.

217
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:19,520
[GIGGLES]

218
00:08:19,520 --> 00:08:20,919
NARRATOR:
Daddy Pig is wearing

219
00:08:20,919 --> 00:08:23,080
his birthday boots.

220
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:25,440
Daddy Pig has found
a little puddle.

221
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:28,400
Let's see
if these boots work.

222
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:31,280
NARRATOR: The puddle is a bit
too little for Daddy Pig.

223
00:08:31,280 --> 00:08:34,520
Hm.
What I need is a big puddle.

224
00:08:34,520 --> 00:08:37,280
Heh. Why not try over here,
Daddy Pig?

225
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:38,319
[PEPPA &amp; GEORGE LAUGHING]

226
00:08:38,319 --> 00:08:40,959
Ooh. What's this?

227
00:08:40,959 --> 00:08:43,520
It's your special
birthday surprise.

228
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:44,640
[GIGGLES]

229
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:46,400
Shh.
Shh.

230
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:47,600
[BOTH LAUGHING]

231
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:50,280
NARRATOR:
What are they up to?

232
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:52,800
[SNORTS]
A big muddy puddle.

233
00:08:52,800 --> 00:08:54,959
Fantastic.

234
00:08:54,959 --> 00:08:56,680
[LAUGHS]

235
00:08:56,680 --> 00:08:59,520
My birthday boots
work perfectly.

236
00:08:59,520 --> 00:09:01,720
[SNORTS]
Would you care to join me

237
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:04,520
in my birthday muddy puddle?
[ALL LAUGHING]

238
00:09:04,520 --> 00:09:07,439
NARRATOR:
Daddy Pig loves jumping up
and down in muddy puddles.

239
00:09:07,439 --> 00:09:10,800
Everyone loves jumping up
and down in muddy puddles.

240
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:13,560
This is my best
birthday ever.

241
00:09:13,560 --> 00:09:15,880
[ALL LAUGHING]

242
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:16,920
[SNORTS]

243
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:19,319
[♪♪♪]

244
00:09:19,319 --> 00:09:22,360
PEPPA:
Sleepover.

245
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:23,880
NARRATOR:
It is nighttime.

246
00:09:23,880 --> 00:09:26,079
Peppa is going
to a sleepover

247
00:09:26,079 --> 00:09:27,720
at Zoe Zebra's house.

248
00:09:27,720 --> 00:09:30,120
[SNORTS, THEN GIGGLES]

249
00:09:31,360 --> 00:09:32,600
Hello, Zoe.

250
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:36,160
Hi, Peppa.
Welcome to my sleepover.

251
00:09:36,160 --> 00:09:38,360
I'll pick you up
in the morning.

252
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:39,520
Bye-bye, Peppa.

253
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:40,760
Bye.

254
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:41,920
[ALL LAUGHING]

255
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:43,400
NARRATOR:
Rebecca, Suzy and Emily

256
00:09:43,400 --> 00:09:44,480
are already here.

257
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:45,439
Hello, everyone.

258
00:09:45,439 --> 00:09:46,839
ALL:
Hello, Peppa.

259
00:09:46,839 --> 00:09:48,360
I've got my teddy.

260
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:49,520
"Hello, everyone."

261
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:50,680
[ALL LAUGHING]

262
00:09:50,680 --> 00:09:52,600
NARRATOR:
Zoe has her toy monkey.

263
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:53,839
[GIBBERS]

264
00:09:53,839 --> 00:09:55,079
Emily has her frog.

265
00:09:55,079 --> 00:09:56,040
[CROAKS]

266
00:09:56,040 --> 00:09:57,600
Suzy has her owl.

267
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:58,959
[HOOTS]

268
00:09:58,959 --> 00:10:01,000
And Rebecca has her carrot.

269
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:04,199
"Carrot, carrot."
[ALL LAUGHING]

270
00:10:04,199 --> 00:10:07,920
NARRATOR: Mr. Zebra
is watching television. 
[CAR ENGINES WHIRRING]

271
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:11,720
That's better.
[PIANO MUSIC PLAYING]

272
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:13,480
I was watching that.

273
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:16,360
But it was a bit boring,
Daddy.

274
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:18,240
[ALL LAUGHING]

275
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:20,439
Daddy Zebra
is going to bed now.

276
00:10:20,439 --> 00:10:23,199
He has to get up early
to deliver the post.

277
00:10:23,199 --> 00:10:25,160
Very well, Mummy Zebra.

278
00:10:25,160 --> 00:10:26,800
Don't stay up too late.

279
00:10:26,800 --> 00:10:29,560
Good night, Mummy.

280
00:10:29,560 --> 00:10:31,600
NARRATOR:
Peppa and her friends
are getting

281
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:33,160
into their sleeping bags.

282
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:36,959
Zoe's baby twin sisters,
Zuzu and Zaza,

283
00:10:36,959 --> 00:10:39,000
want to join
the sleepover too.

284
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,199
[BOTH WHINNY]

285
00:10:40,199 --> 00:10:44,520
The sleepover is only
for big girls.

286
00:10:45,480 --> 00:10:47,199
[BOTH CRYING]

287
00:10:47,199 --> 00:10:50,000
Aw, they're so sweet
and little.

288
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,480
Can they stay?

289
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:55,959
Okay. But you must promise
you'll stay awake.

290
00:10:55,959 --> 00:10:57,560
BOTH:
We promise.

291
00:10:57,560 --> 00:10:58,880
[BOTH GIGGLE]

292
00:10:58,880 --> 00:11:01,319
Wow. A piano.

293
00:11:01,319 --> 00:11:04,600
I'm having lessons.
Listen.

294
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:08,160
♪ Twinkle, twinkle
Little star ♪
[PLAYING OFFKEY NOTES]

295
00:11:08,160 --> 00:11:11,000
Can I have a go?
ALL: And me.

296
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:14,319
ALL: ♪ Twinkle, twinkle
Little star ♪
[PLAYING OFFKEY NOTES]

297
00:11:14,319 --> 00:11:18,760
♪ How I wonder
What you are ♪

298
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:23,880
Shush. You must be quiet
so Daddy Zebra can sleep.

299
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:25,959
Now, into your sleeping bags,
please.

300
00:11:25,959 --> 00:11:27,959
[♪♪♪]

301
00:11:29,240 --> 00:11:31,520
[SNORTS]
What do we do now?

302
00:11:31,520 --> 00:11:37,040
On sleepovers,
there's always a midnight feast.

303
00:11:37,040 --> 00:11:39,319
What's a midnight feast?

304
00:11:39,319 --> 00:11:42,520
We eat things in secret.

305
00:11:42,520 --> 00:11:43,839
ALL: Ooh.

306
00:11:43,839 --> 00:11:46,040
I know where there's food.

307
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:48,680
But we must be very quiet.

308
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:50,040
[♪♪♪]

309
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:51,360
[SUZY &amp; PEPPA GIGGLE]

310
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:52,920
Shh, Suzy.

311
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:54,439
Shh, Peppa.

312
00:11:54,439 --> 00:11:56,480
Quiet.

313
00:11:58,319 --> 00:12:00,360
NARRATOR:
Mummy Zebra has woken up.

314
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:02,280
[SNORTS]
We're going to have

315
00:12:02,280 --> 00:12:05,040
the best midnight feast
ever.

316
00:12:05,040 --> 00:12:06,680
[ALL LAUGH]

317
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:08,600
What's going on?

318
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:10,319
You'll wake Daddy Zebra.

319
00:12:10,319 --> 00:12:15,000
Now, who knows a nice,
gentle bedtime story?

320
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:15,959
Me.

321
00:12:15,959 --> 00:12:17,199
ALL:
And me.

322
00:12:17,199 --> 00:12:18,600
I'll start.

323
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:22,719
Once upon a time,
there was a little fairy.

324
00:12:22,719 --> 00:12:24,760
Now your turn, Peppa.

325
00:12:24,760 --> 00:12:27,480
And she lived in the forest.

326
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:29,439
She was very pretty...

327
00:12:29,439 --> 00:12:31,959
And she had a fairy wand.

328
00:12:31,959 --> 00:12:33,000
Lovely.

329
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:34,560
Your turn, Emily.

330
00:12:34,560 --> 00:12:36,959
Tell us what happens next.

331
00:12:36,959 --> 00:12:39,480
Well, I'm not really sure.

332
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:41,719
Just say anything, Emily.

333
00:12:41,719 --> 00:12:44,480
As long as it's not boring.

334
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:45,880
Okay.

335
00:12:45,880 --> 00:12:50,959
The little fairy met
a big monster, who went...

336
00:12:50,959 --> 00:12:52,240
[TRUMPETS]

337
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:54,280
[ALL SHRIEK]
Too scary.

338
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:55,839
[ALL LAUGHING]

339
00:12:55,839 --> 00:12:58,000
What's all this noise?

340
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:01,000
NARRATOR: Oh, dear.
The noise has woken Mr. Zebra.

341
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:02,800
Sorry, Daddy.

342
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:05,480
There was a story
about a fairy.

343
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:07,280
And a scary monster.

344
00:13:07,280 --> 00:13:11,040
And we want to know
what happens next.

345
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:12,400
Very well.

346
00:13:12,400 --> 00:13:13,439
[CLEARS THROAT]

347
00:13:13,439 --> 00:13:15,839
The monster lifted up

348
00:13:15,839 --> 00:13:18,280
his big, hairy paws

349
00:13:18,280 --> 00:13:19,439
ALL: Ah.

350
00:13:19,439 --> 00:13:23,640
And walked along
on his big, hairy feet.

351
00:13:23,640 --> 00:13:24,880
ALL: Ooh!

352
00:13:24,880 --> 00:13:26,599
And he said:

353
00:13:26,599 --> 00:13:30,800
♪ Twinkle, twinkle
Little star ♪
[PLAYING SONG PERFECTLY]

354
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:35,560
♪ How I wonder
What you are ♪♪

355
00:13:35,560 --> 00:13:37,199
[ALL SNORING]

356
00:13:37,199 --> 00:13:41,880
NARRATOR: Mr. Zebra's song
has sent everyone to sleep.

357
00:13:41,880 --> 00:13:46,079
[♪♪♪]

358
00:13:48,839 --> 00:13:51,439
[♪♪♪]

359
00:13:51,439 --> 00:13:53,319
PEPPA:
Cold Winter Day.

360
00:13:53,319 --> 00:13:54,839
[WIND WHISTLING
THEN PEPPA QUIVERS]

361
00:13:54,839 --> 00:13:56,599
NARRATOR:
It is very cold today.

362
00:13:56,599 --> 00:14:00,319
Peppa and George are wearing
their hats, scarves, coats,

363
00:14:00,319 --> 00:14:02,360
mittens, and boots.

364
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:04,120
[PEPPA &amp; GEORGE LAUGHING]

365
00:14:05,439 --> 00:14:08,079
Look, George.
The trees haven't got leaves.

366
00:14:08,079 --> 00:14:10,719
NARRATOR: In the winter time,
the trees lose their leaves.

367
00:14:10,719 --> 00:14:12,400
[BOTH LAUGHING]

368
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:15,360
NARRATOR: Peppa and George
have found a muddy puddle.

369
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:16,520
BOTH: Ooh.

370
00:14:16,520 --> 00:14:17,959
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George love

371
00:14:17,959 --> 00:14:19,719
jumping up and down
in muddy puddles.

372
00:14:19,719 --> 00:14:20,640
[BOTH GIGGLE]

373
00:14:20,640 --> 00:14:23,160
[SNORTS]
Me first.

374
00:14:23,160 --> 00:14:24,920
Aah! Ugh!

375
00:14:24,920 --> 00:14:28,199
NARRATOR: It is so cold,
the puddle has turned to ice.

376
00:14:28,199 --> 00:14:29,800
It is very slippery.

377
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:31,439
[LAUGHS]

378
00:14:31,439 --> 00:14:33,040
It's not funny.

379
00:14:33,040 --> 00:14:34,640
[CHUCKLES]

380
00:14:34,640 --> 00:14:36,640
NARRATOR:
Here are Mummy Pig
and Daddy Pig.

381
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:39,479
[SNORTS]
Oh, good, a muddy puddle.

382
00:14:39,479 --> 00:14:42,040
NARRATOR:
Daddy Pig loves jumping
in muddy puddles.

383
00:14:42,040 --> 00:14:44,120
Stop, Daddy.

384
00:14:44,120 --> 00:14:45,439
Whoa!

385
00:14:45,439 --> 00:14:46,439
[ALL GASP]

386
00:14:46,439 --> 00:14:49,079
Ho-ho-ho. That was close.

387
00:14:49,079 --> 00:14:51,520
Lucky, I've got
such a good sense of balance.

388
00:14:51,520 --> 00:14:53,360
[ALL LAUGHING]

389
00:14:53,360 --> 00:14:56,479
Daddy,
the puddles are icy today.

390
00:14:56,479 --> 00:14:58,439
We can't jump in them.

391
00:14:58,439 --> 00:15:00,040
[SNORTS]
Never mind.

392
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:02,280
Let's feed some bread
to the ducks.

393
00:15:02,280 --> 00:15:04,000
BOTH:
Hooray! Hee-hee-hee.

394
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,400
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George love
feeding the ducks.

395
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:07,599
[QUACKING]

396
00:15:07,599 --> 00:15:09,400
[SNORTS]
Hello, ducks.

397
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:11,400
We've got some bread
for you.

398
00:15:11,400 --> 00:15:12,520
[QUACKING]

399
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:14,000
NARRATOR:
The ducks like bread.

400
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,360
[PEPPA GIGGLES]

401
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:17,079
Oh.

402
00:15:17,079 --> 00:15:20,560
NARRATOR: It is so cold,
the pond has frozen to ice.

403
00:15:20,560 --> 00:15:22,640
[QUACKING]

404
00:15:24,280 --> 00:15:26,400
NARRATOR:
The ice is very slippery.

405
00:15:26,400 --> 00:15:27,640
[ALL LAUGH]

406
00:15:27,640 --> 00:15:29,920
Sorry for laughing,
Mrs. Duck.

407
00:15:29,920 --> 00:15:31,240
But it did look quite funny.

408
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:32,560
[QUACKS]

409
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:34,439
[QUACKING]

410
00:15:34,439 --> 00:15:37,560
[♪♪♪]

411
00:15:37,560 --> 00:15:39,959
NARRATOR:
It is starting to snow.

412
00:15:39,959 --> 00:15:41,000
Snow!

413
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:42,240
[BOTH LAUGHING]

414
00:15:42,240 --> 00:15:44,800
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George love snow.

415
00:15:44,800 --> 00:15:48,640
[SNORTS]
George, let's catch snowflakes.

416
00:15:48,640 --> 00:15:49,640
[SNORTS]

417
00:15:49,640 --> 00:15:51,360
[BOTH LAUGHING]

418
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:54,040
NARRATOR: Peppa and George
are catching snowflakes.

419
00:15:54,040 --> 00:15:55,319
Ooh.

420
00:15:55,319 --> 00:15:57,479
NARRATOR:
George has caught a snowflake.

421
00:15:57,479 --> 00:15:58,800
[GIGGLES]

422
00:15:58,800 --> 00:16:00,280
NARRATOR:
Peppa has caught a snowflake.

423
00:16:00,280 --> 00:16:01,319
Ooh.

424
00:16:01,319 --> 00:16:03,160
[BOTH GIGGLE]

425
00:16:03,160 --> 00:16:04,199
[BLEATS]

426
00:16:04,199 --> 00:16:05,560
NARRATOR:
Here is Suzy Sheep

427
00:16:05,560 --> 00:16:06,599
on her toboggan.

428
00:16:06,599 --> 00:16:08,199
Whee!

429
00:16:08,199 --> 00:16:09,199
[LAUGHS]

430
00:16:09,199 --> 00:16:10,160
Hello, Peppa.

431
00:16:10,160 --> 00:16:13,199
Wow! Suzy, that looks fun.

432
00:16:13,199 --> 00:16:14,439
[BLEATS]

433
00:16:14,439 --> 00:16:17,040
We're all tobogganing
on the big hill.

434
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:18,599
There's lots of snow there.

435
00:16:18,599 --> 00:16:20,319
[LAUGHING]

436
00:16:20,319 --> 00:16:22,400
[SNORTS]
Shall we climb up the big hill

437
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:24,000
and watch the tobogganing?

438
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:25,479
Yes, please.
[SNORTS]

439
00:16:25,479 --> 00:16:28,040
[BOTH GIGGLING]

440
00:16:28,040 --> 00:16:30,000
[BLEATS]
[ALL LAUGHING]

441
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,839
NARRATOR: Peppa's friends are
tobogganing on the big hill.

442
00:16:32,839 --> 00:16:34,120
Whee!

443
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:35,599
[BARKS]

444
00:16:35,599 --> 00:16:36,920
Yahoo!

445
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:38,439
[GIGGLES]

446
00:16:40,680 --> 00:16:41,599
Whoa!

447
00:16:41,599 --> 00:16:42,880
NARRATOR:
Oh, dear.

448
00:16:42,880 --> 00:16:44,400
George has slipped
on the hill.

449
00:16:44,400 --> 00:16:47,599
You look funny, George.
[GIGGLES]

450
00:16:47,599 --> 00:16:50,280
NARRATOR: George does not think
it is funny.

451
00:16:50,280 --> 00:16:51,920
[CRYING]

452
00:16:54,920 --> 00:16:57,359
It's quite easy
to slip on the hill.

453
00:16:57,359 --> 00:16:59,319
Maybe I should carry George.

454
00:16:59,319 --> 00:17:01,839
Daddy, can you carry me too?

455
00:17:01,839 --> 00:17:04,119
Ho, ho. All right, Peppa.

456
00:17:04,119 --> 00:17:06,839
Just be careful
you don't slip over, Daddy Pig.

457
00:17:06,839 --> 00:17:09,839
Ho, ho.
Don't worry, Mummy Pig.

458
00:17:09,839 --> 00:17:15,000
Remember, I've got
an excellent sense of balance.

459
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:17,800
[ALL LAUGHING]

460
00:17:17,800 --> 00:17:19,560
[BARKS]
Let's have a race.

461
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:20,680
ALL:
Yes!

462
00:17:20,680 --> 00:17:23,560
Ready, steady, go!

463
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:25,399
ALL: Whee!

464
00:17:25,399 --> 00:17:26,839
[ALL LAUGHING]

465
00:17:26,839 --> 00:17:28,879
Here we are.

466
00:17:28,879 --> 00:17:30,360
The top of the big hill.

467
00:17:30,360 --> 00:17:31,919
[SNORTS]
Do be careful

468
00:17:31,919 --> 00:17:33,720
you don't slip, Daddy Pig.

469
00:17:33,720 --> 00:17:34,639
[LAUGHS]

470
00:17:34,639 --> 00:17:37,040
I'm not going to slip.

471
00:17:37,040 --> 00:17:38,399
Whoa!

472
00:17:38,399 --> 00:17:40,399
Whoa!

473
00:17:40,399 --> 00:17:42,080
[BOTH GIGGLING]

474
00:17:42,080 --> 00:17:44,919
Daddy is like
a big toboggan!

475
00:17:44,919 --> 00:17:46,879
[BOTH LAUGHING]

476
00:17:46,879 --> 00:17:48,960
Yahoo!

477
00:17:48,960 --> 00:17:50,960
Whoa!

478
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:54,600
Whee!
We're going to win the race!

479
00:17:54,600 --> 00:17:56,000
Hooray!

480
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:58,240
NARRATOR: Peppa and George
are the winners.

481
00:17:58,240 --> 00:17:59,520
ALL:
Well done, Peppa!

482
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:01,960
[SNORTS]
My Daddy makes

483
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:03,600
a very good toboggan.

484
00:18:03,600 --> 00:18:05,960
[ALL LAUGHING]

485
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:07,840
[SNORTS]
It's not funny.

486
00:18:07,840 --> 00:18:10,360
It is a bit funny,
Daddy Pig.

487
00:18:10,360 --> 00:18:11,800
Hm.

488
00:18:11,800 --> 00:18:13,520
I suppose it is quite funny.

489
00:18:13,520 --> 00:18:14,800
[LAUGHS]

490
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:16,879
[ALL LAUGHING]

491
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:20,040
[♪♪♪]

492
00:18:20,040 --> 00:18:21,040
[GIGGLING AND SNORTING]

493
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:22,800
PEPPA:
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

494
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:24,879
[SNORTS THEN GIGGLES]

495
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:27,800
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

496
00:18:27,800 --> 00:18:29,919
[SNORTING AND GIGGLING]

497
00:18:29,919 --> 00:18:31,760
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

498
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:33,760
[SNORTS AND GIGGLES]

